From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Pablo=20Correa=20G=C3=B3mez?=
 <pabloyoyoista@postmarketos.org>
Date: Mon, 1 Jun 2026 18:55:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sdm670-google-common: enable debug uart
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Enable the debug UART on QUP12 (gpio51/gpio52, routed to the USB-C SBU
pins) and make it serial0, so that the existing stdout-path
"serial0:115200n8" uses it.

No board-level pin configuration is needed on top of the SoC default
(2 mA, bias disabled on TX and RX), which is also what the vendor
kernel uses: its sdm670-pinctrl.dtsi qupv3_se12_2uart_active state sets
drive-strength = <2> and bias-disable on both pins (the sleep state
switches them to GPIO with a pull-down), and the Pixel 3a board DT only
sets status = "ok" on qupv3_se12_2uart without overriding its pins.
Earlier revisions of this patch carried an RX pull-up, matching
sdm845-google-common.dtsi, which has no counterpart downstream.

Tested on the Pixel 3a (sargo) on v7.3-rc4 with an FT232R-based USB-C
SBU debug adapter at 115200 8N1, booting with the SoC default (4 boots)
and with the RX pull-up added back (3 boots). Reading the TLMM
registers back confirmed which bias was active (gpio52 CTL 0x4 without
the pull-up, 0x7 with it). Both behaved the same on every boot: the
console came up, commands typed on the host were echoed back exactly,
an md5sum of a 200-character string typed on the host matched, 200
lines printed by the phone arrived byte-exact (in the 6 boots where
that test ran), SysRq via BREAK worked, and dmesg and the tty counters
(read in 6 of the 7 boots) showed no framing, parity or overrun errors.
In every configuration, including a pull-down, the UART received a
single 0xFF early in boot before the host sent anything, so that byte
is unrelated to the RX bias. All of this was with the adapter attached;
with the adapter's TXD tri-stated the RX line still read high (held by
the adapter) and no bytes arrived in 8 s. An RX pin left floating with
no cable attached was not tested.

Pablo originally tested this on the Pixel 3a with a USB-Cereal board.

Signed-off-by: Pablo Correa Gómez <pabloyoyoista@postmarketos.org>
[sam: drop the board-level RX pull-up after retesting on sargo, as
 requested in the v4 review]
Signed-off-by: Sam Day <me@samcday.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm670-google-common.dtsi | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm670-google-common.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm670-google-common.dtsi
index b4854801a5f5e..79d66fd2d6e41 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm670-google-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm670-google-common.dtsi
@@ -26,7 +26,9 @@
 /delete-node/ &gpu_mem;
 
 / {
-	aliases { };
+	aliases {
+		serial0 = &uart12;
+	};
 
 	battery: battery {
 		compatible = "simple-battery";
@@ -693,6 +695,10 @@ ts-switch-pins {
 	};
 };
 
+&uart12 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &usb_1_hsphy {
 	vdd-supply = <&vreg_l1b_0p925>;
 	vdda-pll-supply = <&vreg_l10a_1p8>;
